Pluto was previously classified as the ninth planet in the solar system, but in 2009, it was reclassified as a dwarf planet by the2 International Astronomical Union (IAU). Dwarf planets in the outer solar system include Pluto, Ceres, Eris, Makemake, and Haumea.

Dwarf planets are distinct from the traditional nine planets because they have not cldden their orbits around the Sun and have not cleared the neighborhood around their orbits of other debris.

